# oracle: dihedral_style class2 at exactly trans (phi = 180): native force zero on the phi terms (B-05)
# oracle-inputs: w87bond_dtrans0.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine thermo agrees to a max relative error of 9.1e-16 with the GPL class2 dihedral port (ORACLE_MEASURE; 7.3e-16 with the analytic one) (forces to the 1e-8 test tolerance)
units real
atom_style full
boundary f f f
read_data w87bond_dtrans0.data
pair_style zero 5.0
pair_coeff * *
bond_style harmonic
bond_coeff * 0 1.5
angle_style harmonic
angle_coeff * 0 110
dihedral_style class2
dihedral_coeff * 100 75 100 70 80 60
dihedral_coeff * mbt 3.5945 0.1704 -0.5490 1.5228
dihedral_coeff * ebt 0.3417 0.3264 -0.9036 0.1368 0.0 -0.8080 1.0119 1.1010
dihedral_coeff * at 0.0 -0.1850 -0.7963 -2.0220 0.0 -0.3991 110.2453 105.1270
dihedral_coeff * aat -13.5271 110.2453 105.1270
dihedral_coeff * bb13 0.0 1.0119 1.1010
improper_style harmonic
improper_coeff * 0 0
thermo_style custom step ebond eangle edihed eimp pe
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run 0
